  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「マスカディンブドウ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%9E%E3%82%B9%E3%82%AB%E3%83%87%E3%82%A3%E3%83%B3%E3%83%96%E3%83%89%E3%82%A6",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 106376052,
      "text": "マスカディンブドウ(英: muscadine、学名 Vitis rotundifolia) は、米国のデラウェアからフロリダを含む東南部から、南部中央のテキサスやオクラホマにかけて自生し、また、栽培されているブドウである。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Vitis rotundifolia」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vitis_rotundifolia",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1368871184,
      "text": "Vitis rotundifolia, or muscadine or swamp grape, is a grapevine species native to the southeastern and south-central United States. The growth range extends from Florida to New Jersey coast, and west to eastern Texas and Oklahoma. It has been extensively cultivated since the 16th century. The plants are well-adapted to their native warm and humid climate; they need fewer chilling hours than better known varieties, and thrive in summer heat."
    }
